onger isoform of Pex5p, Pex5pL, with Pex7p abolishes peroxisome targeting signal type 2 protein import in mammals. Study with a novel Pex5-impaired Chinese hamster ovary cell mutant. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>275</volume>:<fpage>21715</fpage>&#x02013;21721.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10767287</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Nair, D.M., P.E. Purdue, and P. Lazarow. <year>2004</year>. Pex7p translocates in and out of peroxisomes in <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic>. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>167</volume>:<fpage>599</fpage>&#x02013;604.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15545321</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Otera, H., T. Harano, M. Honsho, K. Ghaedi, S. Mukai, A. Tanaka, A. Kawai, N. Shimizu, and Y. Fujiki. <year>2000</year>. The mammalian peroxin Pex5pL, the longer isoform of the mobile peroxisome targeting signal (PTS) type 1 transporter, translocates the Pex7p.PTS2 protein complex into peroxisomes via its initial docking site, Pex14p. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>275</volume>:<fpage>21703</fpage>&#x02013;21714.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10767286</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Otera, H., K. Setoguchi, M. Hamasaki, T. Kumashiro, N. Shimizu, and Y. Fujiki. <year>2002</year>. Peroxisomal targeting signal receptor Pex5p interacts with cargoes and import machinery components in a spatiotemporally differentiated manner: conserved Pex5p WXXXF/Y motifs are critical for matrix protein import. <source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <volume>22</volume>:<fpage>1639</fpage>&#x02013;1655.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11865044</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Otzen, M., D. Wang, M.G. Lunenborg, and I.J. van der Klei. <year>2005</year>. <italic>Hansenula polymorpha</italic> Pex20p is an oligomer that binds the peroxisomal targeting signal 2 (PTS2). <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <vol